  "narration": {
    "title": "The Dodgers Hold, the East Wobbles",
    "intro": "Los Angeles still sits atop the power ranking with a plus-150 run differential and no challengers in sight. Behind them, the surprise is movement in the other direction: the Braves and Yankees both went 3-7 over their last ten and slid down the board.",
    "power_lead": "The Dodgers stay at number one, but the Marlins are the story underneath, 8-2 over their last ten and up to fourth despite a run differential of just plus-11. The Braves dropped three spots and the Yankees five, both undone by a rough week.",
    "offense_lead": "The Dodgers lead the team-OPS board too, at .788, the only club clear of the pack. Pittsburgh sneaking in at third, ahead of Colorado and Washington, is the kind of name you don't expect this high.",
    "staffs_lead": "Milwaukee owns the starter-ERA ranking at 3.21, fueled by Jacob Misiorowski's 1.45 mark and a form needle pinned at 100. The Dodgers (3.27) and Rays (3.34) round out the top three, proof that pitching is carrying the contenders."
  }
